--- A list pushed as an item of a list of lists keeps its items apart from
--- the outer list's: joined, a row's ints had been ranged as the rows, and
--- a doubling through a list of rows stayed a 64-bit multiply that
--- overflowed compiled. And a nested collect whose rows hold ints past 64
--- bits is grown at each depth, where the outer list had been converted
--- again from rows it no longer held (Rosetta Code, Bell numbers, Abelian
--- sandpile model).
fn doubled[row]
    return push[[], row[-1] * 2]

rows = push[[], push[[], 1]]
while len[rows] lt 70
    rows = push[rows, doubled[rows[-1]]]
log[rows[-1][0]]

g = for r in range[2]
    row = for c in range[2]
        0
    row
g[0][0] = 2 ^ 70
log[g]
